    {
      "@id": "concept:disability-discrimination-and-other-human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2009-sch-2-sec-7-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "7 Discrimination in relation to associates",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/disability-discrimination-and-other-human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2009#sch-2-sec-7-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "disability-discrimination-and-other-human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "disability-discrimination-and-other-human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2009.pdf, p.12",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This Act applies in relation to a person who has an associate with a\ndisability in the same way as it applies in relation to a person with\nthe disability.\nExample: It is unlawful, under section 15, for an employer to discriminate\nagainst an employee on the ground of a disability of any of the\nemployee’s associates.\n\nDisability discrimination  Schedule 2\nAmendments commencing 28 days after Royal Assent  Part 1\n\nDisability Discrimination and Other Human Rights Legislation Amendment Act\n2009          9\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), but without limiting that\nsubsection, this Act has effect in relation to a person who has an\nassociate with a disability as if:\n\n(a) each reference to something being done or needed because of\na disability were a reference to the thing being done or\nneeded because of the fact that the person has an associate\nwith the disability; and\n\n(b) each other reference to a disability were a reference to the\ndisability of the associate.\n\n(3) This section does not apply to section 53 or 54 (combat duties and\npeacekeeping services) or subsection 54A(2) or (3) (assistance\nanimals).\nNote:\nThe combined effect of sections 7 and 8 is that this Act applies in\nrelation to a person who has an associate who has a carer, assistant,\nassistance animal or disability aid in the same way as it applies in\nrelation to a person with a disability.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This Act applies in relation to a person who has an associate with a\ndisability in the same way as it applies in relation to a person with\nthe disability.\nExample: It is unlawful, under section 15, for an employer to discriminate\nagainst an employee on the ground of a disability of any of the\nemployee’s associates.\n\nDisability discrimination  Schedule 2\nAmendments commencing 28 days after Royal Assent  Part 1\n\nDisability Discrimination and Other Human Rights Legislation Amendment Act\n2009          9\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), but without limiting that\nsubsection, this Act has effect in relation to a person who has an\nassociate with a disability as if:\n\n(a) each reference to something being done or needed because of\na disability were a reference to the thing being done or\nneeded because of the fact that the person has an associate\nwith the disability; and\n\n(b) each other reference to a disability were a reference to the\ndisability of the associate.\n\n(3) This section does not apply to section 53 or 54 (combat duties and\npeacekeeping services) or subsection 54A(2) or (3) (assistance\nanimals).\nNote:\nThe combined effect of sections 7 and 8 is that this Act applies in\nrelation to a person who has an associate who has a carer, assistant,\nassistance animal or disability aid in the same way as it applies in\nrelation to a person with a disability.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:disability-discrimination-and-other-human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2009-sch-2-sec-7-2-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:disability-discrimination-and-other-human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2009-sch-2-sec-7-2-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:disability-discrimination-and-other-human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2009-sch-2-sec-7-2-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "114e7bef50f29c5b9321d1cbda6d83a3af11f67062c25e062a5fcfd8966601a9"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/disability-discrimination-and-other-human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2009#sch-2-sec-7-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "7 Discrimination in relation to associates",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 12,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This Act applies in relation to a person who has an associate with a\ndisability in the same way as it applies in relation to a person with\nthe disability.\nExample: It is unlawful, under section 15, for an employer to discriminate\nagainst an employee on the ground of a disability of any of the\nemployee’s associates.\n\nDisability discrimination  Schedule 2\nAmendments commencing 28 days after Royal Assent  Part 1\n\nDisability Discrimination and Other Human Rights Legislation Amendment Act\n2009          9\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), but without limiting that\nsubsection, this Act has effect in relation to a person who has an\nassociate with a disability as if:\n\n(a) each reference to something being done or needed because of\na disability were a reference to the thing being done or\nneeded because of the fact that the person has an associate\nwith the disability; and\n\n(b) each other reference to a disability were a reference to the\ndisability of the associate.\n\n(3) This section does not apply to section 53 or 54 (combat duties and\npeacekeeping services) or subsection 54A(2) or (3) (assistance\nanimals).\nNote:\nThe combined effect of sections 7 and 8 is that this Act applies in\nrelation to a person who has an associate who has a carer, assistant,\nassistance animal or disability aid in the same way as it applies in\nrelation to a person with a disability."
    },
    {
