      },
      "dc:source": "disability-discrimination-and-other-human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2009.pdf, p.12",
      "values:originalText": "(3) This section does not apply to section 53 or 54 (combat duties and\npeacekeeping services) or subsection 54A(2) or (3) (assistance\nanimals).\nNote:\nThe combined effect of sections 7 and 8 is that this Act applies in\nrelation to a person who has an associate who has a carer, assistant,\nassistance animal or disability aid in the same way as it applies in\nrelation to a person with a disability.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) This section does not apply to section 53 or 54 (combat duties and\npeacekeeping services) or subsection 54A(2) or (3) (assistance\nanimals).\nNote:\nThe combined effect of sections 7 and 8 is that this Act applies in\nrelation to a person who has an associate who has a carer, assistant,\nassistance animal or disability aid in the same way as it applies in\nrelation to a person with a disability.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:disability-discrimination-and-other-human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2009-sch-2-sec-7-2"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:disability-discrimination-and-other-human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2009-sch-2-sec-7-2-ss-3-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0f72d94c81444c00868880ae4c3e1555790b55830853c0a7a6f0c37b829333e3",
      "skos:note": "Exempts certain sections from the Act's application"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/disability-discrimination-and-other-human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2009#sch-2-sec-7-2-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "7(3) Discrimination in relation to associates",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 12,
      "values:originalText": "(3) This section does not apply to section 53 or 54 (combat duties and\npeacekeeping services) or subsection 54A(2) or (3) (assistance\nanimals).\nNote:\nThe combined effect of sections 7 and 8 is that this Act applies in\nrelation to a person who has an associate who has a carer, assistant,\nassistance animal or disability aid in the same way as it applies in\nrelation to a person with a disability."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:disability-discrimination-and-other-human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2009-sch-2-sec-7-2-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:disability-discrimination-and-other-human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2009-sch-2-sec-7-2-ss-3"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:disability-discrimination-and-other-human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2009-sch-2-sec-8-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "8 Discrimination in relation to carers, assistants, assistance animals",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/disability-discrimination-and-other-human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2009#sch-2-sec-8-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "disability-discrimination-and-other-human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "disability-discrimination-and-other-human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2009.pdf, p.13",
      "values:originalText": "and disability aids\n\n(1) This Act applies in relation to having a carer, assistant, assistance\nanimal or disability aid in the same way as it applies in relation to\nhaving a disability.\nExample: For the purposes of section 5 (direct discrimination), circumstances\nare not materially different because of the fact that a person with a\ndisability requires adjustments for the person’s carer, assistant,\nassistance animal or disability aid (see subsection 5(3)).\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), but without limiting that\nsubsection, this Act has effect in relation to a person with a\ndisability who has a carer, assistant, assistance animal or disability\naid as if:\n\n(a) each reference to something being done or needed because of\na disability were a reference to the thing being done or\nneeded because of the fact that the person has the carer,\nassistant, animal or aid; and\n\n(b) each other reference to a disability were a reference to the\ncarer, assistant, animal or aid.\n\n(3) This section does not apply to section 48 (infectious diseases) or\nsection 54A (exemptions in relation to assistance animals).\n\nSchedule 2  Disability discrimination",
      "skos:definition": "and disability aids\n\n(1) This Act applies in relation to having a carer, assistant, assistance\nanimal or disability aid in the same way as it applies in relation to\nhaving a disability.\nExample: For the purposes of section 5 (direct discrimination), circumstances\nare not materially different because of the fact that a person with a\ndisability requires adjustments for the person’s carer, assistant,\nassistance animal or disability aid (see subsection 5(3)).\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), but without limiting that\nsubsection, this Act has effect in relation to a person with a\ndisability who has a carer, assistant, assistance animal or disability\naid as if:\n\n(a) each reference to something being done or needed because of\na disability were a reference to the thing being done or\nneeded because of the fact that the person has the carer,\nassistant, animal or aid; and\n\n(b) each other reference to a disability were a reference to the\ncarer, assistant, animal or aid.\n\n(3) This section does not apply to section 48 (infectious diseases) or\nsection 54A (exemptions in relation to assistance animals).\n\nSchedule 2  Disability discrimination",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:disability-discrimination-and-other-human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2009-sch-2-sec-8-3-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:disability-discrimination-and-other-human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2009-sch-2-sec-8-3-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:disability-discrimination-and-other-human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2009-sch-2-sec-8-3-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f96055928d11f3d92b73c55db1c5356e07f7bc72bcd1d84d4cf82ac68f29b60e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/disability-discrimination-and-other-human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2009#sch-2-sec-8-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "8 Discrimination in relation to carers, assistants, assistance animals",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 13,
      "values:originalText": "and disability aids\n\n(1) This Act applies in relation to having a carer, assistant, assistance\nanimal or disability aid in the same way as it applies in relation to\nhaving a disability.\nExample: For the purposes of section 5 (direct discrimination), circumstances\nare not materially different because of the fact that a person with a\ndisability requires adjustments for the person’s carer, assistant,\nassistance animal or disability aid (see subsection 5(3)).\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), but without limiting that\nsubsection, this Act has effect in relation to a person with a\ndisability who has a carer, assistant, assistance animal or disability\naid as if:\n\n(a) each reference to something being done or needed because of\na disability were a reference to the thing being done or\nneeded because of the fact that the person has the carer,\nassistant, animal or aid; and\n\n(b) each other reference to a disability were a reference to the\ncarer, assistant, animal or aid.\n\n(3) This section does not apply to section 48 (infectious diseases) or\nsection 54A (exemptions in relation to assistance animals).\n\nSchedule 2  Disability discrimination"
    },
